The programme committee of the kernel summit would like to invite a
representative of the Kernel Janitors to attend the Kernel Summit.
However, instead of us picking someone, we're going to turn the problem
over to you.  So choose one person, by whatever means you think
appropriate (having secured their consent of course, and having made
sure they can actually go to the Kernel Summit, 16-18 July in Ottawa,
Canada) and send their name to the kernel summit programme committee
<ksummit-2006-pc@thunk.org>. 

Whoever you pick should be prepared to make a contribution to the whole
of the kernel summit ... and since this is the first time we've tried to
make a particular community of people pick their representative, so
we'll be watching to see if it's a successful model we can follow for
future years.

Thanks

James Bottomley





